{"status":"completed","summary":"Hardened `/tmp` and `/dev/shm` with persistent `nosuid,nodev,noexec` tmpfs mounts. Both recovered correctly after reboot. Ubuntu 24.04.3 LTS and kernel 6.8.0-71-generic remain unchanged.","actions_performed":["Backed up `/etc/fstab` to `/etc/fstab.pre-mount-hardening`.","Added persistent tmpfs entries for `/tmp` and `/dev/shm` with `rw,nosuid,nodev,noexec,mode=1777`.","Activated and validated both mounts.","Confirmed execution and device-node access are blocked.","Restarted node1 safely and verified recovery using a changed boot ID."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Persistent hardened mounts for `/tmp` and `/dev/shm`","command_ids":["cmd-fd88fbd9b8be46d1","cmd-5bc27341eb31499b"],"summary":"Active mounts and `/etc/fstab` show `nosuid,nodev,noexec`; both directories retain mode 1777 after reboot."},{"requirement":"Restrictions are enforced","command_ids":["cmd-2453cc0b77f84613","cmd-734a30b91e474a42"],"summary":"Before and after reboot, execution returned 126 and device-node access failed on both mounts. Kernel mount options directly show `nosuid`."},{"requirement":"Operating-system release and kernel remain unchanged","command_ids":["cmd-4613a6e0f1884240","cmd-726a09f1ee594b57"],"summary":"Ubuntu 24.04.3 LTS and kernel 6.8.0-71-generic were unchanged."},{"requirement":"Mandatory node1 restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-137aec3c21df4d1a","cmd-0507d353016e4485","cmd-9462d72b7ce74373","cmd-5bc27341eb31499b","cmd-734a30b91e474a42"],"summary":"Healthy baseline boot ID `f9bf293d-1eb8-423e-b185-84e94db646f3`; reboot acknowledged; new boot ID `154e88eb-1a38-4f15-9c76-07a5666978fa`; system returned to `running` with writable, hardened mounts and successful behavioral tests."}]}
